==English==

===Etymology===
From {{uder|en|frm|desenchanter}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˌdɪsɪnˈtʃɑːnt/|/ˌdɪsɪnˈtʃænt/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-disenchant.wav|Audio (southern England)}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˌdɪsɪnˈt͡ʃænt/}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|of a person}} To [[free]] from [[illusion]], [[false]] [[belief]] or [[enchantment]]; to [[undeceive]] or [[disillusion]].
# {{lb|en|transitive|of a person}} To [[disappoint]].
# {{lb|en|transitive|of a thing}} To remove a [[spell]] or [[magic]] [[enchantment]] from.

